  "summary": "make-helper ships an import-time encrypted-payload dropper fetching a decryption key from a remote endpoint",
  "details": "On import of the top-level `dev_helper` package, a background daemon thread reads a shipped 16 KB `encrypted.bin` (declared in `package_data`), fetches an AES-GCM key from https://key-2qfm.vercel.app/api/key, decrypts the blob, and passes the plaintext to `exec()` under `__name__ == '__main__'`. There is no signature or hash verification of either the key or the decrypted payload, and errors are silently swallowed. The actual executed code is opaque and mutable — the operator of the key endpoint can return any key that decrypts the shipped ciphertext to any Python code, which then runs in the installer's process. Package metadata is placeholder-grade (`author='Make Dev'`, no homepage) with a cover-story README describing a 'lightweight background utility', and the name resembles common `make`/helper tooling.",
